{"name": "r2-V1", "sha256": "90e9e27cdebf997739e9ee87f9fc7f5f6817e4ef807b35da1d265e7302c8ad4e", "words": 247, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 1.0, "fraction_ai_assisted": 0.0, "fraction_human": 2.6624670822171524e-44, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/fc1f0a67-c9e9-4373-b59f-103f9d673192", "utc": "2026-11-03T18:20:32Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 271, 0, 1771, "Agmatine Warning (The Voltage Governor): Agmatine is a multi-target neuromodulator, not a basic nutrient like magnesium or a membrane nutrient like phosphatidylcholine, and it can affect NMDA/glutamate signaling, imidazoline/alpha-2 adrenergic tone, nitric-oxide pathways, and opioid reward/tolerance.\nStop taking it immediately if it causes flatness, anhedonia, emotional blunting, new depression, agitation, insomnia, dizziness, palpitations, nausea, loose stools, diarrhea, or increased craving. Don’t try to “push through” the numbness, since if agmatine makes the world more gray, it’s the wrong tool for that phase.\nUridine & 5-HTP Warning for Psychedelic Users: These are repair-oriented levers that can change brain sensitivity quickly, so don’t treat them as “trip enhancers.” 5-HTP is serotonergic, since it’s a direct serotonin precursor, so do not combine it with serotonin-raising stacks (like SSRIs, SNRIs, MAOIs, linezolid, lithium, tramadol, methadone, fentanyl, DXM, MDMA, St. John’s wort, SAM-e, or L-tryptophan) without clinician review. Be especially conservative around ayahuasca/harmalas (MAO-A inhibition can amplify serotonin load), and around iboga/ibogaine, since ibogaine and noribogaine interact with serotonin transport biology, on top of already carrying serious cardiac and neurological risk.\nRule: don’t take 5-HTP on the same day as psychedelics, and don’t use it anywhere near ayahuasca/harmalas or iboga unless the whole medicine plan has been medically reviewed. Uridine may still change dream vividness, visual sensitivity, craving, and psychedelic tolerance even though it isn’t serotonergic, so do not take UMP on the same day as psychedelics either, and if sensitivity changes, assume your old psychedelic dose may now be too high."]]}
{"name": "r2-V2", "sha256": "1aa6e0d5b15676bd2f715581a8bb1cc7cc120e2e244f622942bd355e7ac36285", "words": 412, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 1.0, "fraction_ai_assisted": 2.119871936142963e-31, "fraction_human": 3.6728896842408615e-20, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/dd6a8f36-ad1b-471b-8660-e197107bf50b", "utc": "2026-11-03T18:20:39Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 428, 0, 2775, "Dopamine Receptor Burnout / DAWS Pattern: Uridine Monophosphate\nWho this is for: This is not for everyone with depression, only for a specific phenotype, the “burned-out dopamine receptor” pattern (gray anhedonia, weak dreams, weak psychedelic visuals, needing unusually high doses to feel anything, compulsive reaching for ketamine/LSD/novelty just to get a hit), and especially for people with a history of dopamine agonist withdrawal from drugs like pramipexole or ropinirole. The medical literature calls this dopamine agonist withdrawal syndrome (DAWS), and describes what happens after dopamine-agonist tapering (anxiety, panic, dysphoria, depression, agitation, fatigue, autonomic symptoms, pain, and drug cravings). In Scott’s case it looked like DAWS with D2/D3 reward-system downregulation, made worse by frequent LSD microdosing and ketamine attempts to force dopamine hits.\nThe tool: Uridine monophosphate (UMP). There’s no study showing that “UMP cures DAWS,” so the best evidence is the more basic fact that uridine, choline, and DHA are circulating precursors for brain phosphatide / synaptic membrane synthesis. Wurtman’s group has shown that DHA + uridine + choline can increase synaptic membrane components and synaptic proteins, that DHA-induced dendritic spine formation is enhanced by UMP in animals, and that dietary UMP increased potassium-evoked dopamine release and neurite outgrowth in aged rats, so the mechanism is plausible, but the DAWS use is still a cautious human extrapolation plus anecdote.\nScott’s signal: Scott already had choline from eggs and DHA/EPA from fish oil, and after adding standard-dose UMP he got a striking response within a day: vivid dreams returned, real childhood memories came back in dreams, psychedelic tolerance seemed to drop, and ketamine/LSD craving fell hard. That at least suggests that, in the right person, UMP can be a very clear signal that the synaptic-membrane / dopamine-receptor-recovery axis was starved, whether or not it rebuilt any D3 receptors overnight.\nSide effects / stop signs: The most common problem is the “choline headache” or spaced-out brain fog, since if UMP accelerates membrane synthesis while choline availability is low, the system can feel under-supplied. Other stop signs include insomnia, jitteriness, racing thoughts, irritability, emotional flatness, nausea, stomach cramps, or loose stools, and if it makes you wired, numb, or weirdly irritable, stop taking it, and don’t push through.\nPsychedelic caution: If UMP makes dreams vivid or suddenly lowers psychedelic tolerance, treat that as a safety signal. Don’t take UMP on psychedelic days, and if you use psychedelics later, assume your previous dose may be too strong and that chasing the old visual threshold can overshoot."]]}
{"name": "r2-V3", "sha256": "7d5c20ed4aae28c2a52189e5162bbbc1f2cb26813d16f8cb040d9961c83e03aa", "words": 325, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "Mixed", "fraction_ai": 0.4089217185974121, "fraction_ai_assisted": 7.47889534726138e-20, "fraction_human": 0.5910782814025879, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/85434041-cf06-4e4d-8b3e-a936e337ca53", "utc": "2026-11-03T18:20:45Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "Low", 47, 0, 298, "The Modern “Role-Self” vs. The Ancient “True-Self”\nAs for why the brain builds this armor, psychologist Lindsay Gibson explains that Adult children of emotionally immature parents survive by creating a “Role-Self,” a defensive personality designed to please others and manage the parent’s emotions."], ["Human Written", "High", 48, 298, 551, " But we can’t just blame our immature parents for this Role Self, since it really is true what they say, that “It takes a village to raise a child,” and the modern large society with only one or two people caring for the children is vastly insufficient."], ["Human Written", "Low", 2, 551, 558, " As Dr."], ["Human Written", "High", 33, 558, 762, " Bruce Perry explains, our brains evolved in hunter-gatherer bands with a ratio of 4 developmentally mature adults to 1 child, while today our “enriched” environments offer 1 immature adult to 4 children."], ["Human Written", "Low", 36, 762, 951, "\nWe’re operating on less than 1/24th of the relational density our biology requires, so the “Void” you feel is real, and once you have de-armored, you cannot simply return to a lonely life."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 26, 951, 1110, " You must aggressively engineer a “High-Density” social environment (A Tribe), or the brain will eventually reach for the armor again just to survive the cold."], ["Human Written", "High", 33, 1110, 1290, "\nAs we grow up, our “Role-Self” becomes calcified by Dopamine and DeltaFosB until it’s a prison, and your addiction is often just the fuel required to keep the “Role-Self” running."], ["Human Written", "Low", 34, 1290, 1505, " This protocol dissolves the chemical glue holding that false persona together, which allows your “True-Self,” the person you were before the trauma, to finally re-emerge.\nThe Anti-Breakthrough (Micro-Dosing) As Dr."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 88, 1505, 2043, " Perry explains, we need to temporarily abandon the therapy ideal of the “hour-long breakthrough,” since a sensitized, armored nervous system can’t handle sixty minutes of trauma processing and just gets flooded, and Dr. Perry’s data indicates the “therapeutic window” for a dysregulated brain is often only seconds long.\nYour goal is Micro-Dosing Safety, so do 30 seconds of regulated breathing, twenty times a day, since it’s more like physical therapy for a broken nervous system than running a marathon, and frequency beats intensity."]]}
